===============================================================================
HOW TO ATTRIBUTE
===============================================================================

Keep the credit visible wherever CARA is used, published or handed to a client. In a
deployed copy of the application this means leaving the footer credit in place. In a
document, report or deck derived from CARA, use:

  CARA, Copilot Adoption Readiness Assessment, by Jelmar Groot.
  https://github.com/jellebelletje/CARA
  Licensed under CC BY 4.0.

If you changed the questions, the rubric or the scoring, say so. The licence requires
you to indicate that changes were made, and it protects you as much as it protects the
original: someone reading your adapted version should not attribute your edits to
someone else.

CARA is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Microsoft. Microsoft, Microsoft
365, Copilot, Purview and Viva are trademarks of the Microsoft group of companies, and
are referred to here only to identify the products an assessment concerns.
